{"claims":[{"excerpt":"Uitgevouwen was Webb nog niet klaar voor routinewetenschap","claim":"Webb’s completed deployment did not mean it was yet ready for routine science.","category":"chronology","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"After six months: “Science operations!” Webb began its science mission and started to conduct routine science operations.","narrative":"uitgevouwen zijn een belangrijke mijlpaal was, niet het einde van Webbs weg naar wetenschappelijke operaties","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The source distinguishes completing deployment from beginning routine science operations six months later.","materiality":"Central distinction of the piece."},{"excerpt":"De James Webb-ruimtetelescoop moest opgevouwen in de kuip van de Ariane 5-raket passen: zijn operationele configuratie was daarvoor te groot.","claim":"Webb’s operational configuration was too large for the Ariane 5 fairing, so it was designed to fit there in a folded, compact launch configuration.","category":"technical","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"The Ariane 5 launch vehicle's rocket fairing has a diameter of approximately 18 ft (5.4 m) x 43ft (13m) tall. Webb was designed to fold compactly to fit into the fairing.","narrative":"Webb was ontworpen om opgevouwen in de Ariane 5-kuip te passen.","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"This accurately summarizes the stated size constraint and folded launch design.","materiality":"Relevant context for why deployment was necessary."},{"excerpt":"Het uitvouwen omvatte veel stappen en mogelijke faalpunten.","claim":"Webb’s deployment involved many steps and possible points of failure.","category":"quantity","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"There were over 50 major deployment steps, with 178 release mechanisms that had to perform perfectly or any one of over 300 single points of failure could have diminished or crippled the mission.","narrative":"De uitvouwing omvatte veel stappen en mogelijke faalpunten","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"“Veel” accurately conveys the source’s figures without claiming a different count.","materiality":"Conveys the complexity and stakes of deployment."},{"excerpt":"Die risicovolle fase verliep soepel.","claim":"The risky deployment phase proceeded smoothly.","category":"outcome","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"Webb's deployment was completed with remarkable smoothness.","narrative":"de uitvouwing verliep soepel","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The source explicitly characterizes deployment as remarkably smooth, while also describing substantial risks.","materiality":"Materially rules out an implication that deployment failed."},{"excerpt":"In de tweede week waren de spiegels uitgeklapt en vergrendeld en had Webb zijn operationele configuratie bereikt.","claim":"In the second week, Webb’s mirrors had unfolded and latched, bringing the telescope to its fully deployed operational configuration.","category":"technical","label":"F1 minor immaterial imprecision","evidence":"During the second week after launch, we finished deploying the telescope structures by unfolding and latching the secondary mirror tripod and rotating and latching the two primary mirror wings. This brought Webb into its fully deployed operational configuration.","narrative":"In de tweede week waren de spiegels uitgevouwen en vergrendeld en had Webb zijn operationele configuratie bereikt.","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"new_distortion","explanation":"The source specifies that the secondary-mirror tripod unfolded and latched, while the two primary-mirror wings rotated and latched. Saying the mirrors themselves unfolded is an imprecise shorthand for deploying those structures, but the stated timing and resulting configuration are correct.","materiality":"Minor technical imprecision; it does not change the main timeline or outcome."},{"excerpt":"Dat was een belangrijke mijlpaal, maar nog niet het einde van de ingebruikname.","claim":"Reaching the fully deployed operational configuration was a milestone, but commissioning was not yet complete.","category":"interpretation","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"This brought Webb into its fully deployed operational configuration. ... The remaining five months of commissioning were all about aligning the optics and calibrating the scientific instruments.","narrative":"was een belangrijke mijlpaal, niet het einde van Webbs weg naar wetenschappelijke operaties","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The source describes deployment as completing the deployed configuration and then details five further months of commissioning.","materiality":"The distinction between deployment and commissioning is central."},{"excerpt":"De telescoop koelde daarna wekenlang af.","claim":"After deployment, the telescope cooled for several weeks.","category":"chronology","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"The telescope and scientific instruments started to cool rapidly in the shade of the sunshield, but it took several weeks for them to cool all the way down and reach stable temperatures.","narrative":"afkoeling ... liepen door tijdens de ingebruikname van zes maanden","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The source places cooldown in the first month after deployment and says it took several weeks.","materiality":"Relevant commissioning-stage chronology."},{"excerpt":"Vervolgens gingen maanden op aan het uitlijnen van de spiegels en het kalibreren van de instrumenten.","claim":"After cooldown, months were spent aligning Webb’s mirrors and calibrating its instruments.","category":"chronology","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"The remaining five months of commissioning were all about aligning the optics and calibrating the scientific instruments. ... In the second, third and fourth months: Initial optics checkouts, and telescope alignment. ... In the fifth and sixth months: Calibration and completion of commissioning.","narrative":"spiegeluitlijning en instrumentkalibratie liepen door tijdens de ingebruikname van zes maanden","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The source assigns alignment to months two through four and instrument calibration to months five and six; the piece summarizes these stages accurately.","materiality":"Establishes what occupied the period between deployment and routine science."},{"excerpt":"Na zes maanden ingebruikname begon Webb aan routinewetenschap.","claim":"Webb began routine science operations after six months of commissioning.","category":"chronology","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"After six months: “Science operations!” Webb began its science mission and started to conduct routine science operations.","narrative":"Na zes maanden begon Webb aan routinewetenschap.","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The stated endpoint and activity match the source.","materiality":"Defines the endpoint of the timeline."},{"excerpt":"De uitvouwing was dus voltooid voordat de telescoop klaar was voor die fase.","claim":"Webb’s deployment was complete before it was ready to begin routine science operations.","category":"chronology","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"During the second week after launch, we finished deploying the telescope structures ... This brought Webb into its fully deployed operational configuration. ... After six months: “Science operations!” Webb began its science mission and started to conduct routine science operations.","narrative":"De tijdlijn maakt het onderscheid duidelijk tussen de voltooide uitvouwing en het afronden van de ingebruikname.","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The source places completion of deployment in the second week and routine science operations after six months.","materiality":"Summarizes the piece’s central chronological relationship."}]}

